{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Count-based deployment properties (U1) will leverage Spring's existing PropertyPlaceholderConfigurer/PropertySourcesPlaceholderConfigurer mechanism, extending the deployment property resolver to recognize a dedicated 'count' token and instantiate N copies of the module with shared environment variables.",
    "gh-pages branch (U2) will be configured as an orphan branch using the standard GitHub Pages approach; documentation generation will be wired into the existing Maven/Gradle build with Asciidoctor or MkDocs output, published via a CI job that pushes generated HTML to gh-pages.",
    "Kafka binder fix (U3) will be approached as a targeted bug fix in the spring-cloud-stream-binder-kafka module, with diagnostic logging added first to confirm the binding failure mode before code changes; backward compatibility with existing Kafka client versions will be preserved.",
    "Architecture reference documentation (U4) will be written in AsciiDoc and structured as a side-by-side comparison of 1.x and 2.x deployment topologies (local, Cloud Foundry, Kubernetes, Yarn), leveraging the existing reference guide template.",
    "Concourse CI study (U5) is scoped as a research task: explore pipelines, tasks, resources, and fly CLI; produce a written findings document with recommendations; no production pipeline implementation is included.",
    "RxJava processor module (U6) will follow the existing Spring Cloud Stream processor pattern (Function/Consumer/Supplier) and use RxJava's Flowable/Observable adapters; the module will be a thin wrapper around the reactive-stream contract to avoid duplicating binder code.",
    "Shell server banner (U7) will be generated as ASCII art via patorjk.com/taag, stored as a banner.txt resource, and wired into the Spring Boot Banner mechanism via spring.main.banner-location.",
    "Cloud Foundry deployment section (U8) will be added to the project README following the existing section structure, with concrete steps and a link to the canonical docs.",
    "All activities assume a single senior developer working full-time; code review, unit tests, and minor integration verification are folded into each activity's estimate rather than treated as a separate line item."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "{{count}}, {{N}}, {{gh_pages}}, and {{Kafka}} are template variables from the story tracker; the intended values are 'count' (property name), N (an integer count of instances), 'gh-pages' (branch name), and 'Kafka' (the Kafka binder for Spring Cloud Stream).",
    "The Spring Cloud Data Flow (s-c-d) and Spring Cloud Stream / Spring Cloud Stream Microservices (s-c-s / s-c-s-m) codebases, build infrastructure, and CI are already in place; no bootstrapping of repos, build systems, or environments is required.",
    "An 8-hour workday is used as the unit of effort; estimates are effort (person-days), not calendar duration.",
    "U5 (Concourse CI study) is treated as a research-and-document deliverable, not an implementation; it therefore requires a shorter time than the coding stories.",
    "No large-scale refactoring, breaking API changes, or new framework subsystems are implied by the stories; each story fits within the existing architecture.",
    "The Kafka binder bug is of moderate complexity (not a fundamental redesign); if the actual bug proves deeper, estimates would need to be revised upward.",
    "Documentation is published using the project's existing static-site/doc generation toolchain; no new doc-system selection is required."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "U1.1",
      "activity_name": "Design count property substitution",
      "activity_description": "Define the property syntax (e.g., deployer.<module>.count=N), the substitution rules, and how the resolved count propagates through the deployment launcher to spawn N module instances sharing the same environment variables.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U1.2",
      "activity_name": "Implement count property handling",
      "activity_description": "Extend the deployment property resolver, update the module deployment path to iterate N times while sharing env vars, and wire the new property through the relevant configurers/listeners.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U1.3",
      "activity_name": "Test count-based deployment",
      "activity_description": "Add unit and integration tests covering count=1, count>1, count with shared env vars, and invalid count values; verify the launcher creates the correct number of module instances.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U2.1",
      "activity_name": "Configure gh-pages branch",
      "activity_description": "Create the orphan gh-pages branch in the s-c-d and s-c-s-m repositories, set up the branch as the GitHub Pages source, and add a README placeholder so the page renders correctly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U2.2",
      "activity_name": "Set up documentation publishing workflow",
      "activity_description": "Configure the build to generate HTML docs and a CI job (Travis/CircleCI) that pushes the generated output to the gh-pages branch on merge to main.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U3.1",
      "activity_name": "Diagnose Kafka binder binding failure",
      "activity_description": "Reproduce the binding failure against an operational Kafka broker, capture broker/client logs, and isolate the root cause within the spring-cloud-stream-binder-kafka module.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U3.2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Kafka binder fix",
      "activity_description": "Apply the targeted code change to address the diagnosed issue, preserving compatibility with supported Kafka client versions and existing configuration properties.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U3.3",
      "activity_name": "Test Kafka binder fix",
      "activity_description": "Add regression tests for the fixed scenario, run the binder test suite against a live or testcontainers-based Kafka broker, and verify successful binding.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U4.1",
      "activity_name": "Analyze 1.x vs 2.x deployment architectures",
      "activity_description": "Review both codebases, identify the key structural differences (server, skipper, deployers, stream DSL, batch/task handling), and outline the comparison structure.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U4.2",
      "activity_name": "Write architecture reference documentation",
      "activity_description": "Author the AsciiDoc reference page describing 1.x and 2.x deployment differences, with diagrams (PlantUML) and concrete examples for each target platform.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U5.1",
      "activity_name": "Study Concourse CI",
      "activity_description": "Explore Concourse CI concepts (pipelines, tasks, resources, jobs, the fly CLI), review sample pipelines, and evaluate fit for s-c-d's CI/CD needs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U5.2",
      "activity_name": "Document Concourse CI study findings",
      "activity_description": "Produce a written summary covering capabilities, integration options, migration effort, and recommendations for adopting Concourse CI in s-c-d.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U6.1",
      "activity_name": "Design RxJava processor module",
      "activity_description": "Define the module's API surface (function signatures, RxJava Flowable/Observable types), its relationship to the spring-cloud-stream reactive binder, and configuration properties.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U6.2",
      "activity_name": "Implement RxJava processor module",
      "activity_description": "Implement the processor module with adapters between RxJava types and the reactive-streams contract used by Spring Cloud Stream, register it as a Spring configuration class.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U6.3",
      "activity_name": "Test RxJava processor module",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests verifying the RxJava processor correctly publishes/subscribes through the binder, including back-pressure and error-propagation cases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U7.1",
      "activity_name": "Generate and configure shell server banner",
      "activity_description": "Generate the ASCII art banner via patorjk.com/taag, store it as banner.txt on the classpath, and configure spring.main.banner-location in the shell server so the banner displays at boot.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "U8.1",
      "activity_name": "Document Running on Cloud Foundry in README",
      "activity_description": "Add a 'Running on Cloud Foundry' section to the s-c-d README, covering prerequisites, manifest, deployment steps, and a link to the detailed docs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 15.5
  }
}
